TASK-189 runtime survey harness: the Settings window, every pane, light and
dark, in the states that change layout, plus the window-sizing checks added
in part 1. It measures, it fixes nothing. Temporary code, never committed to
Detour/. Since part 1 it uses SettingsPaneViewController and
SettingsWindowController.screenUsableHeightOverride, so it applies on top of
part 1 or later. The patch also adds the run tools under .task189/ (removed
again by the revert). Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task189-survey-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    OUT=<an empty folder>
    LOCK_CHECK=<lock probe> .task189/watch.sh "$OUT" &   # shoots each "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>"
                                  # line of $OUT/verify.log with screencapture -x -o -l
    .task189/run.sh "$OUT" [app args]  # DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify189, prints the pid;
                                  # e.g. -AppleShowScrollBars Always for legacy scrollers
    # wait for "done" in $OUT/verify.log (about 130 s), then kill THAT pid only
    python3 .task189/analyze.py "$OUT" > "$OUT/analysis.txt"
    python3 .task189/borders.py "$OUT" > "$OUT/borders.txt"   # list border vs background pixels
    python3 .task189/sheets.py "$OUT"   # contact sheets in $OUT/sheets
    python3 .task189/compare.py BEFORE AFTER "$OUT/sheets" profiles extensions
                                  # before/after sheets, each state side by side
    git apply -R docs/harness/task189-survey-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    rm -r -- ~/Library/Application\ Support/DetourVerify189

Start from a fresh DetourVerify189 (the script adds spaces, profiles and
extensions). For the real second-screen check, run the TASK-110 virtual display
(docs/task-110/vdisplay.m, 1600x1000 pt) before launching and kill it after;
without it the "profiles-on-short-screen" state logs "skipped".
TASK189_SWITCH_ONLY=1 runs only launch, open Settings and a set of pane
switches (no captures; run without the watcher), for quick animation checks.

The harness opens Settings 2 s after launch and steps through the states, each
captured light then dark (NSApp.appearance), waiting for each PNG before the
next step. For every capture it writes $OUT/<state>-<mode>.json: each visible
view under the window's content view (class, text, frame, alignment rect and
first baseline in window coordinates, intrinsic and needed text size,
line-break mode, hasAmbiguousLayout, scroll document vs clip size, stack
spacing and order, grid rows with hidden flags), and the pane's natural height,
minimum, the window's contentMin/MaxSize and the screen override. analyze.py
derives clips (frame cut by a clip view or the content, from the frames:
visibleRect is useless because macOS 14+ views do not clip to bounds), text
that does not fit, overlaps between on-screen leaves, scroll overflow, gaps
between stack items and grid rows, label-vs-control centre and baseline
offsets, the grid's top against the list's (and, since part 2, a column
stack's top against the list's: COLUMN lines), grid label-column widths and pane
margins. Unsatisfiable-constraint logs: `log show --predicate
'processIdentifier == <pid>'`, grep "Unable to simultaneously".
States: general; spaces default / long space + long profile name / 19
spaces; extensions none / one tall extension (only-tall) / the same
uninstalled through the pane's own Uninstall button, its alert answered from
a timer in the modal run loop (UNINSTALL lines: content height before and
after); profiles normal / Private / custom UA + isolation
warning / 4 external-app permissions; extensions one (unpacked) / long name +
long description + 22 permissions + 4 hosts + optional + options page (CRX
with update URL) / pending-permissions banner / 15 installed (one-permission extension selected); profiles with
15 extension switches / everything shown / same scrolled to the end / Private
with extensions; content blocking on / off. Then the sizing checks (part 1):
pane switches sampled from the window server every 10 ms on a background
thread (SWITCH lines: distinct heights, top edge kept); posted mouse drags on
the bottom edge past both bounds and on the left and right edges (DRAG lines);
spaces-many-dragged (after the drags); a 600 pt screen through
screenUsableHeightOverride: profiles-capped / profiles-capped-scrolled /
spaces-capped / extensions-capped; the override removed plus a posted
didChangeScreenParametersNotification (SCREEN lines); profiles-on-short-screen
(the window moved onto the virtual display, then back). Extensions are
installed through ExtensionManager.install(from:options:) from folders the
harness writes, so the permission rows are recorded as a real install records them.

Known false positives in analyze.py: "VCLIP NSButton ... frame=[48, 25, 24,
19]" (the list's minus button, alignment rect vs frame) and
"_NSLayerBasedFillColorView" OUTSIDE-CONTENT / PAST-PARENT (a 0-wide view of
the system scroll pocket at the top of the pane's scroll view); the
"BackdropView / NSScrollPocket / NSBanner" OVERLAPs are the table header's
system views; spaces-many-dragged's 2 pt OVERLAP of the list separator with a
row half scrolled under it. borders.py samples list containers and, since
part 2, the bordered groups (SettingsGroupBoxView).

